3 UAN - areas with archaeological finds
The spatial delineation of UAN reflects the current state of knowledge of the area from the perspective of archaeology and is divided into four categories:
UAN I - areas with positively proven and further safely presumed occurrence of archaeological finds;
UAN II - areas where the occurrence of archaeological finds has not yet been positively proven, but certain indications support it: the probability of the occurrence of archaeological finds is 51-100%;
UAN III - areas where the occurrence of archaeological finds has not yet been identified and positively documented, and for the time being no indications support it, but the area in question may have been settled or otherwise used by humans, and therefore there is a 50% probability of the occurrence of archaeological finds. This is therefore the area of the entire Czech Republic excluding UAN I, II, and IV;
UAN IV - areas where the probability of the occurrence of archaeological finds is unrealistic - all mined areas - quarries, brickworks, sand pits, etc.
§ 21 - 24 of Act No. 20/1987 Coll. - In the entire area of interest in categories UAN I - III, the provisions resulting from the Act must be observed. This means that it is necessary to respect § 22 of Act No. 20/1987 Coll. on State Monument Care in its current version in the space of UAN I, II, and III, i.e., builders are already from the preparation of the construction, i.e., the intention, to carry out any earthworks in which an archaeological find in the sense of § 23 may be discovered, obliged to notify this intention to the Archaeological Institute of the Czech Academy of Sciences and to enable it or an organization authorized to conduct archaeological research to carry out a rescue archaeological research in the affected area.

3 UAN - areas with archaeological finds
The spatial delineation of UAN reflects the current state of knowledge of the area from the perspective of archaeology and is divided into four categories:
UAN I - areas with positively proven and further safely presumed occurrence of archaeological finds;
UAN II - areas where the occurrence of archaeological finds has not yet been positively proven, but certain indications support it: the probability of the occurrence of archaeological finds is 51-100%;
UAN III - areas where the occurrence of archaeological finds has not yet been recognized and positively documented, and no indications currently support it, but the area in question may have been settled or otherwise used by humans, and therefore there is a 50% probability of the occurrence of archaeological finds. This therefore refers to the entire territory of the Czech Republic excluding UAN I, II, and IV;
UAN IV - areas where the probability of the occurrence of archaeological finds is unrealistic - all excavated areas - quarries, brickworks, sand pits, etc.
§ 21 - 24 of Act No. 20/1987 Coll. - In the entire area of interest in categories UAN I - III, the provisions resulting from the Act must be observed. This means that it is necessary to respect § 22 of Act No. 20/1987 Coll. on State Monument Care in its current version in the space of UAN I, II, and III, i.e., builders are already from the preparation of the construction, i.e., the intention, to carry out any earthworks in which an archaeological find in the sense of § 23 may be discovered, obliged to notify this intention to the Archaeological Institute of the Czech Academy of Sciences and to enable it or an organization authorized to conduct archaeological research to carry out a rescue archaeological research in the affected area.
